### A minimal command set

```bash
bun install --frozen-lockfile
bun run build
bun run test
```

Keep the generated site in `dist/`. A failed build or test should stop the release rather than publish a partial output.

### Example configuration

```json
{
  "name": "studio-website",
  "pages_build_output_dir": "dist"
}
```

The project name is illustrative. Use the actual Cloudflare project when deploying.

### A useful check for content

```javascript
const required = ["title", "summary", "images"];

for (const project of projects) {
  for (const field of required) {
    if (!project[field]) {
      throw new Error(`Missing ${field} in ${project.slug}`);
    }
  }
}
```

This catches missing fields. It does not check whether the writing or images are appropriate; those still need a person to review them.

Use the official [Cloudflare Pages documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/) for deployment details. The local build command is `bun run build`, not a browser dependency.
